er_own":21.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Greif, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, produces and sells industrial packaging products and services worldwide. It operates in four segments: Customized Polymer Solutions; Durable Metal Solutions; Sustainable Fiber Solutions; and Innovative Closure Solutions. The Customized Polymer Solutions segment produces and sells polymer-based packaging products, such as plastic drums, rigid intermediate bulk containers, and small plastics for chemicals, food and beverage, agricultural, pharmaceutical, and mineral products industries. The Durable Metal Solutions segment offers metal-based packaging products, including various steel drums for the chemicals, petroleum, agriculture, and paints and coatings industries. The Sustainable Fiber Solutions segment provides fiber-based packaging products comprising fibre drums, uncoated recycled board, coated recycled board, tubes and cores, and specialty partitions made from uncoated recycled board and coated recycled board to packaging, automotive, construction, food and beverage, and building products industries. The Innovative Closure Solutions segment offers complimentary packaging products, such as paints, linings, and closure systems for industrial packaging products and related services. The company manufactures and sells rigid industrial packaging products, such as steel, fibre and plastic drums, rigid intermediate bulk containers, jerrycans and other small plastics, closure systems for industrial packaging products, water bottles, and remanufactured and reconditioned industrial containers, as well as offers container life cycle management, logistics, warehousing, and other packaging services. It also purchases and sells recycled fiber; and produces and sells adhesives. Greif, Inc. was founded in 1877 and is headquartered in Delaware, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ole G. Rosgaard | President, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $365K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Greif Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.6B market cap on $4.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -12% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 8% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $123M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.6\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 9.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 32% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.31778913272238357},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $8.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 20% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Greif Bros. (NYSE:GEF.B) Sees Strong Trading Volume \u2013 Here\u2019s Why","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/15/greif-bros-nysegef-b-sees-strong-trading-volume-heres-why.html","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794770822.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.926,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (GEF.B)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/14/Understanding_Momentum_Shift